<div class="definition-preview">
<div class="definition-preview-top"><h3 id="{{DEFINITION_PREFIX}}-title">Complete customer-data export</h3></div>
<div class="definition-meaning"><div class="definition-hero"><figure class="definition-illustration"><img src="assets/definition-completeness-v1.png" alt="Two record sheets with matching row markers; one required marker is missing from the export." width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>One missing required identifier makes this criterion fail.</figcaption></figure><div class="definition-core"><p>Within the identifier-coverage scope, a customer-data export is complete if and only if every required row identifier from the declared account, filters and fixed source snapshot is present in its saved output.</p>
</div></div>
<div class="definition-formal"><code>Complete(E, S, A, F) ⇔ RequiredIds(S, A, F) ⊆ ExportedIds(E)</code></div></div>
<details class="lens-record-detail definition-record-detail definition-structure-detail"><summary>Read the full definition</summary>
<div class="definition-symbols"><p class="record-label">Symbols in the formula</p><dl class="definition-notation"><div><dt><var>E</var></dt><dd>The saved export output being assessed.</dd></div><div><dt><var>S</var></dt><dd>The identified, fixed source snapshot.</dd></div><div><dt><var>A</var></dt><dd>The declared customer account.</dd></div><div><dt><var>F</var></dt><dd>The declared filters that select rows within that account.</dd></div><div><dt><code>RequiredIds(S, A, F)</code></dt><dd>The identifiers of rows in snapshot <var>S</var> that belong to account <var>A</var> and satisfy filters <var>F</var>.</dd></div><div><dt><code>ExportedIds(E)</code></dt><dd>The identifiers of rows present in output <var>E</var>.</dd></div></dl><p>The export is complete when every identifier selected by the account and filters in that fixed snapshot is present in its output.</p></div>
<p class="record-label definition-scope-label">Scope and boundaries</p><dl class="definition-fields"><div><dt>Applicability</dt><dd>Identifier-coverage assessments of customer-data exports from a fixed input snapshot, for the declared account and filters.</dd></div><div><dt>Exclusions</dt><dd>Data-access permission, value accuracy, duplicate or extra rows, response time, permission to deploy a fix and incident closure are assessed under their own criteria.</dd></div><div><dt>Semantic owner</dt><dd>The customer-data service owner, responsible for this meaning within the export assessment scope.</dd></div><div><dt>Boundary conditions</dt><dd>Each required row has a stable identifier, and the snapshot and output use the same identity rule. The sets record presence of identifiers. Account membership and filters are evaluated against the snapshot’s values. A different snapshot, account or set of filters requires its own assessment.</dd></div></dl>
<div class="definition-voices"><dl><div><dt>Plain-language voice</dt><dd>Every required row identifier is present in the output.</dd></div><div><dt>Domain-context voice</dt><dd>While investigating the {{CASE_ACCOUNT}} export incident, the agent compares the identifiers required by snapshot {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}} and filter <code>{{CASE_FILTERS}}</code> with those in saved output {{CASE_OUTPUT}}. This assesses the reported omission.</dd></div></dl></div>
<div class="definition-review-fields"><dl class="definition-fields"><div><dt>Stable identity</dt><dd><code>example.definition.complete-customer-data-export</code> · version {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}}.</dd></div><div><dt>Authority scope</dt><dd>Customer-data export completeness assessments for this illustrative service.</dd></div><div><dt>Testable conditions</dt><dd>If every required identifier is present, the completeness criterion is satisfied. If any required identifier is absent, it is not satisfied. Without an identifiable fixed input snapshot, the assessment remains unestablished.</dd></div><div><dt>Boundaries</dt><dd>The explanatory voices preserve the governing meaning. A changed meaning requires a successor definition version and the responsible owner’s acceptance. This definition supplies no permission to read data or deploy software.</dd></div><div><dt>Primary consumers</dt><dd>The row-comparison method, the agent’s assessment and the owner’s review of the completeness claim.</dd></div><div><dt>Sources and evidence</dt><dd>The extraction requirement is invented for this article. The later evidence example identifies inputs, output and method; those records support a result assessed under this definition.</dd></div><div><dt>Registry and index</dt><dd>A real acceptance would select this exact version in the definition registry and synchronize its lookup index. This example is not registered.</dd></div><div><dt>Drift and challenge route</dt><dd>The service owner reviews whether later assessments preserve this meaning. Bring contradictory evidence or a proposed change of meaning to that owner through the recorded review route.</dd></div></dl>
</div><p class="definition-image-credit">Illustration generated with imagegen. <a href="research/definition-card-images.json">Prompt and asset record</a>.</p></details>
